From 4a9a82f4c342063753381ccca894aca499bfae8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:51:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 322/324] gallium/pvr: real mipmaps

Mipmapped textures stored level 0 only and reported last_level 0, so the
state tracker kept reallocating them and copying levels the driver could
not map (61 "transfer_map ... mipmapped" errors per glmark2 run, in
texture-filter=mipmap and terrain), and generate_mipmap was a no-op.

- A mip chain in a colour target format is twiddled and laid out as the
  Vulkan driver's pvr_image: power-of-two levels back to back, room for
  the full chain down to 1x1, no TFBC.
- Texture descriptors sample the view's levels (num_mip_levels,
  mipmaps_present, baselevel) when the sampler has a mip filter; the mip
  filter bit is set for LINEAR only, the LOD clamps get the quirk 51025
  rounding and the min/mag filter override as in the Vulkan sampler.
  Without a mip filter the view's first level is described alone.
- Rendering into a level (FBO on a level, uploads, generation): the PBE
  gets the level address, pitch and allocated extents.
- transfer_map on a level goes through a linear staging copy of the level
  (no read back when the whole level is replaced).
- generate_mipmap renders each level from the one above (2x2 box filter
  in the load background); caps generate_mipmap and npot_textures.
- Whole-level resource_copy_region / blit between colour targets is one
  GPU render instead of two staging copies.
- HWRT data set cache 16 (a chain renders every level size), end-of-tile
  programs cached per target address (32).
- Formats the PBE cannot write keep level 0 only (logged once).

gltri GLTRI_MIP (per-level uploads, 2048x2048 and 600x360, LINEAR_MIPMAP_
NEAREST and _LINEAR), GLTRI_GENMIP and GLTRI_MIPRT (clear into a level
through an FBO) match zink checksum for checksum; all earlier modes
unchanged. Full glmark2: 0 errors (61 before), score 727 (728); terrain,
shadow and refract drop (27->11, 317->185, 107->37) because their large
targets are now really rendered (previous commit) and refract generates
its mip chain every frame.
